<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria to offer 200 mln levs 2-yr T-notes Nov 8.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria to offer 200 mln levs 2-yr T-notes Nov 8.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer 200 million levs of two-year floater coupon T-notes at an auction on Friday, the central bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue will be offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The semi-annual coupon was set equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15 percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	 BG 2032796125</p>
<p> Par value	    200 million levs</p>
<p> Auction date	 November 8, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	   November 14, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	November 12, 1998</p>
<p> Coupon payments:   May 15, 1997; November 13, 1997;</p>
<p>			  May 14, 1998; November 12, 1998</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
